Z||000009||BAM-BAM||01-01-2001||11:39 AM||||    Cooter, I installed Eibach lowering sprins front and rear. The Eibachs were not the same as the stock. The eibachs are about an 3/4-1" lower than stock and the drop is more than 1" when installed. Some one must have sold you a bogus set of lowering springs. <BR>    Philphine, there will be parts that need to be replaced. Rule of thumb (IMHO) while you there change it all; bushings balljoints shocks, endlinks, everything. Once you tear into it you'll see why, who wants to go through that again. If you have the lowering springs use them. If you want a lower ride that's a little firmer, I know a forum member who has aa set of WS6 springs for sale. They are the stiffest option WS6 Springs made for 85. You could buy them and cut them. LMK<P>  Peace, B2 OUT!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Don B. <BR>85GT<BR>Eibach/KYB Susp.<BR>Mr.Mikes 500 series seats,headliner! MOMO Commando Steering Wheel, White Face Race Style Gauges And Soon To Be More!!! YEAH BABY-YEAH||||reg||1
